    "nickname": "5DN1L",
    "content": "There's indeed some overlap with the existing Scrabble puzzle https://www.codingame.com/training/medium/scrabble . For the record, the main differences at present (on 23 August 2026) are:\n\n* The original puzzle doesn't require a word to use all the available tiles in the hand, whereas your puzzle requires an exact match of the letters in the hand (anagram matching).\n\n* Your puzzle requires evaluating several hands (groups of scrambled letters), whereas the original puzzle requires evaluating only one hand.\n\n* Your puzzle has high and low modes, whereas the original puzzle always selects the word with the highest score.\n\n* The original puzzle uses the first appearance in the dictionary as its tie-breaker, whereas your puzzle uses alphabetical order.\n\n* The upper bound on the number of words in the dictionary is much smaller in your puzzle.\n\nThe first four points will require some rewriting of the solution to the existing puzzle to address this one. The first point, in particular, will simplify the matching logic a lot.",
    "codingamerHandle": "bbb8f47ea4601179303c20acdbf5fb6c1904782",
    "avatar": 134264063920528,
    "elapsedTime": 121432000
